  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 1236 AM MDT Sun Aug 23 2026\n\nUpper level high pressure drifts back westward into the swrn\nU.S. during the week, with mid/upper level flow becoming\nslightly more nwly through the period. Still not much change\nexpected Tue, with another round of afternoon/evening storms \nfocused over the mountains, drifting onto the plains in the \nevening. Weak front may then drop south south through the plains\nlate Tue into Wed, potentially enhancing convection over the \neastern mountains and across the plains on Wed, as enhanced \neasterly upslope winds behind the front refresh low level \nmoisture. Max temps will drift downward a few degf by Wed, as \nridge shifts subtly west and moisture increases. Slow transition\nto drier weather starts Thu as ridge gets far enough west to \ncut-off deeper mid-level moisture, but still expect the usual \ncrop of afternoon/evening storms, most numerous eastern \nmountains and plains. Drier and warmer weather then in store for\nFriday into next weekend, though we never completely flush the \nmoisture out of the area, so at least isolated afternoon/evening\nconvection will continue each day, especially over the \nmountains.",
